/*******************************************************************************
* \file ppca_linker_ns_ram.icf
* \version 1.000
*
* Linker file for the IAR compiler.
*
* The main purpose of the linker script is to describe how the sections in the
* input files should be mapped into the output file, and to control the memory
* layout of the output file.
*
* \note This linker script supports 80KB PPCA Core0 application execution
* across memory regions M0 (32KB), M2 (32KB), and M3 (16KB).
* The memory remap feature enables contiguous execution mapping.
*
* Memory Layout:
*   - M0 (Code): 0x00000000 - 0x00007FFF (32KB)
*   - M2 (Code): 0x00008000 - 0x0000FFFF (32KB)
*   - M3 (Code): 0x00010000 - 0x00013FFF (16KB)
*   - M1 (Data): 0x20000000 - 0x20003FFF (16KB, shared memory)
*   - M4 (Data): 0x20040000 - 0x20043FFF (16KB, shared memory)
*
* \note The entry point is fixed and starts at 0x02010000. The valid application
* image should be placed there.
*
* \note The linker files included with the PDL template projects must be generic
* and handle all common use cases. Your project may not use every section
* defined in the linker files. In that case you may see warnings during the
* build process. In your project, you can simply comment out or remove the
* relevant code in the linker file.
*
********************************************************************************
